From: Brad Barnett <127794626+bdbarnett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:39:58 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] esp32/boards/ESP32_GENERIC_S31: USB device off; a board
 built on it chooses its USB and REPL.

The generic board turns on the native USB device. The overlay's USB device
code (the streaming endpoints, USB networking) is written for TinyUSB 0.21,
and the S31 builds the component registry's TinyUSB 0.19.0~3, the one that
supports the chip, so it is off here until our TinyUSB supports the S31.
The REPL stays on the UART.

A board whose USB-C connector is wired to USB Serial/JTAG, such as the
Waveshare ESP32-S31-Zero, needs that on, and its header is included before
this one. Each setting is now defined here only if the board hasn't.
---
 ports/esp32/boards/ESP32_GENERIC_S31/mpconfigboard.h | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ports/esp32/boards/ESP32_GENERIC_S31/mpconfigboard.h b/ports/esp32/boards/ESP32_GENERIC_S31/mpconfigboard.h
index 09f8adb2d..dbaf08b5f 100644
--- a/ports/esp32/boards/ESP32_GENERIC_S31/mpconfigboard.h
+++ b/ports/esp32/boards/ESP32_GENERIC_S31/mpconfigboard.h
@@ -4,10 +4,20 @@
 #endif
 #define MICROPY_HW_MCU_NAME                 "ESP32-S31"
 
-#define MICROPY_HW_ENABLE_USBDEV              (1)
+#ifndef MICROPY_HW_ENABLE_USBDEV
+// Off: the overlay's USB device code needs TinyUSB 0.21, and the S31 builds
+// the component registry's TinyUSB 0.19, the one that supports the chip.
+#define MICROPY_HW_ENABLE_USBDEV              (0)
+#endif
+#ifndef MICROPY_HW_USB_CDC_DTR_RTS_BOOTLOADER
 #define MICROPY_HW_USB_CDC_DTR_RTS_BOOTLOADER (0)
+#endif
+#ifndef MICROPY_HW_ESP_USB_SERIAL_JTAG
 #define MICROPY_HW_ESP_USB_SERIAL_JTAG        (0)
+#endif
+#ifndef MICROPY_HW_ENABLE_UART_REPL
 #define MICROPY_HW_ENABLE_UART_REPL           (1)
+#endif
 
 #define MICROPY_HW_I2C0_SCL                   (1)
 #define MICROPY_HW_I2C0_SDA                   (0)
